WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.636
A correct join key must match the level of the
relationship Suppose

00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:10.494
your target result is one row per admission You
already have patients

00:00:10.507 --> 00:00:16.376
joined to admissions correctly Now imagine adding
lab results by patient

00:00:16.402 --> 00:00:21.339
ID only If that patient has several admissions and
several lab tests

00:00:21.628 --> 00:00:25.984
every admission can pair with every lab for that
patient The admission

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:31.193
grain is destroyed The deeper question is whether a
lab belongs to

00:00:31.206 --> 00:00:35.364
the patient generally to one admission or to a more
specific encounter

00:00:36.301 --> 00:00:41.169
The database design should tell you This is why
knowing that two

00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:44.788
tables both contain patient ID is not enough
evidence that joining them

00:00:44.814 --> 00:00:50.551
only on patient ID is analytically correct Before
adding another table

00:00:50.827 --> 00:00:53.761
restate the target grain and ask whether the new
table is at

00:00:53.788 --> 00:00:58.290
the same level If not aggregate it filter it or use
a

00:00:58.303 --> 00:01:00.080
more specific relationship key
